From 947bc436aabf248d50c7fa19da1bdc0917ae5fc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:36:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 173/181] hydra: the viewport shows render settings' vars, not
 depth (K-129)

GetDefaultAovDescriptor() answered color, depth, normal and the ids only.
Houdini's viewport, on a stage with render settings, binds the product's
render vars and drops those without a descriptor: with Karma's `C` as the
beauty (Cycles Render Settings LOP) it asked for depth, primId and
instanceId alone and displayed depth. Any other name now gets a float4
descriptor; the session resolves it as husk does. Checked in the viewport:
C, Emit and Combined_key bound, the image in colour.
---
 src/hydra/render_delegate.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/hydra/render_delegate.cpp b/src/hydra/render_delegate.cpp
index b8e19f30..b15a6bbb 100644
--- a/src/hydra/render_delegate.cpp
+++ b/src/hydra/render_delegate.cpp
@@ -525,6 +525,13 @@ HdAovDescriptor HdCyclesDelegate::GetDefaultAovDescriptor(const TfToken &name) c
   {
     return HdAovDescriptor(HdFormatInt32, false, VtValue(-1));
   }
+  /* Any other name is a render var the session resolves (session.cpp: `C`, Cycles and Karma
+   * pass names, light groups, shader AOVs). Houdini's viewport drops every render var of the
+   * render settings it gets no descriptor for: with Karma's `C` as the beauty it asked for
+   * depth alone and showed it as the image. */
+  if (!name.IsEmpty()) {
+    return HdAovDescriptor(HdFormatFloat32Vec4, false, VtValue(GfVec4f(0.0f)));
+  }
 
   return HdAovDescriptor();
 }
